{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1233565-enhanced-item-merit","id":1233565,"title":"Enhanced Item Merit","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-09T18:32:19-07:00","id":1233565,"title":"Enhanced Item Merit","content":"Hi! In Enhanced Item Merit, it says that the effects is related with Matter Arcane and that it's possible raise Durability of some itens.<br /> So, is possible to raise an Armor Rating with this Merit? For example, wear a reinforced clothes 1/0 and with the Merit purchase with 3 dot points and raise its Armor to 3/0?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9723-winchester","name":"winchester","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-09T21:44:22-07:00","id":1233603,"title":"","content":"Sure, 3-dot Enhanced Item with the Matter 3 Aegis spell on it.<br /> <br /> The only problem is figuring out how much Potency the relinquished spell is allowed to have for its dot cost.<br /> There's no direction, but the safest answer is Potency = Merit Dots spent on the spell.<br /> <br /> So for that 3-dot item, you get 3 points to distribute between raising the general/balistic Armor of the item by 1 per.<br /> <br /> It's not fantastic, but it can give you a tailored suit, hoodie or tracksuit capable of soaking up damage almost as well as Chainmail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12644-herbertisbestbert","name":"HerbertIsBestBert","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12644_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"312"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-10T03:49:10-07:00","id":1233644,"title":"","content":"Yes. You can have a bulletproof suit made of normal yet magical fabric.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}